<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46692" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδύν-ω</span></b> , aor. 1
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥδῡνα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					175e
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.
				24
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, aor. 1
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδύνθην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					90
				</span></i>
			: pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥδυσμαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
				</span></i>
			 (v. infr.), inf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδύνθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phot.
				</span></i>
			: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδύς</span>):—<i>season</i> a dish, c. acc.,
				[<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόκκυγας</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Epich.
				164
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
				</span></i>
			l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρόμμυον . . οὐ μόνον σῖτον ἀλλὰ καὶ
					ποτὸν ἡδύνει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					4.8
				</span></i>
			; <i>make pleasant</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γεῦσιν,
				οἴνους</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Od.</u>
				9
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				10
			</span></i>; even of salt (cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡδονή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11
				</span></i>
			), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				359a34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ. θῶπας λόγους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
				</span></i>
			l.c.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ποιητὴς ἡ. τὸ ἄτοπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Po.</u>
					1460b2
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν ἡδυσμένην μοῦσαν παραδέξῃ ἐν
					μέλεσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					607a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1449b28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1340b17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς λόγους ἡδύνεσθαι ἄν τι ὑπὸ τῶν
					φθόγγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					6.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>delight, coax, gratify</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόλαξ ἥδυνέ τινα λόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diph.
					24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ. τὴν ἀκοήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Comp.</u>
					14
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, Timo<i><span class="en">
				17
			</span></i>.</div>
